  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "The product of two positive numbers is \\(9.\\) The reciprocal of one of these numbers is \\(4\\) times the reciprocal of the other number. What is the sum of the two numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{10}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{20}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Label the positive numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) so that\n\\[\n\\frac1x=\\frac4y.\n\\]\nBecause \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are nonzero, multiplying by \\(xy\\) gives \\(y=4x\\). This expresses both numbers using one unknown, so their product condition becomes\n\\[\n9=xy=x(4x)=4x^2.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(x^2=\\frac94\\). Since \\(x>0\\), we take the positive root \\(x=\\frac32\\); the negative root is excluded. Then \\(y=4\\cdot\\frac32=6\\). Their sum is\n\\[\n\\frac32+6=\\boxed{\\frac{15}{2}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
